{
  "_comment": "The one table behind delay causes in the app and the server (task: causes in the selected language). trv: Trafikverket announcement codes (TrainAnnouncement.Deviation[].Code) -> locale key cause.<slug>; trvText: Trafikverket texts that have no code in the list; dt: Digitraffic cause codes (category A, detailed A1, third A101) -> key, null when no honest short translation exists (the resolver then uses the parent code, then shows the Finnish name). kind: cause (says why a train is late) or notice (carriage, platform or service note, not a reason). verified: false = the en/sv wording in packages/shared/locales is ours and not yet reviewed; Trafikverket's own Swedish text (sv) is theirs. Read by packages/shared/src/delayCauses.ts and ClackCore/Logic/DelayCauses.swift (copied by scripts/ios/sync_assets.py).",
  "_source": {
    "trv": "Trafikverket Open API, object type ReasonCode (group Annonseringstexter, non-deleted ANA001-ANA155), Level3Description is the announced Swedish text; fetched 2026-10-24. ANA066 (Test) and ANA099 ({Fritext}) are left out; ANA200 and up are bus-stop and gate names, not causes. The \"Orsaker nya principer\" group (IBT01, JVA01 ...) is the planners' internal cause tree and is never announced, so it is not mapped.",
    "trvText": "The earlier hard-coded table in the app: texts without a code in the ReasonCode list.",
    "dt": "Digitraffic metadata cause-category-codes, detailed-cause-category-codes and third-cause-category-codes (https://rata.digitraffic.fi/api/v1/metadata/...); the Finnish names (fi) are theirs, only in Finnish. All en/sv wording is a translation by Clack and is unverified."
  },
  "skippedTrv": {
    "ANA066": "Test",
    "ANA099": "{Fritext}: free text, shown as written"
  },
